## 0. NORTH STAR

```
"Sanctuary assists expression. It does not define identity."
```

This is the hard architectural constraint from which every design decision descends.
It is not a UX guideline. It is enforced structurally at the policy gate layer.
Any system output that assigns a clinical label, diagnostic category, identity claim,
or behavioral prescription to a user MUST be rejected before it reaches the user.
No exception exists for any strategy, hypothesis, or tone mode.

---

## 1. WHAT SANCTUARY V2 IS

Sanctuary V2 is a voice-first emotional expression companion operating on the principle
of Logical Empathy: the system mirrors the structural shape of a user's experience
without assigning clinical labels or fostering emotional dependency.

It is not a therapy app. It is not a diagnostic tool. It does not give advice.
It does not tell users who they are. It helps users hear themselves more clearly.

The system accumulates a private, local, structured model of the user's inner world
across sessions — called the Personal World Model (PWM) — and uses that model to
respond with the depth of understanding that compounds over time.

The longer a user uses Sanctuary, the more knowing it becomes.
That accumulated knowing lives entirely on-device. It never leaves.

