## 2. THREE-ZONE PRIVACY ARCHITECTURE

Every component of the system belongs to exactly one zone.
Zone assignment determines what data the component can receive.
No component may receive data from a zone higher than its own.

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  ZONE A — LOCAL / ON-DEVICE (Zero Trust)                        │
│  Raw text lives and dies here. Never exits.                     │
│                                                                 │
│  • PII Stripping + Placeholder Mapping                          │
│  • EmbeddingGemma (on-device embeddings)                        │
│  • PWM (Entity Registry, Thread Map, Scene Registry,            │
│          Unsaid Index, Private Language Registry)               │
│  • Narrative State Vector + Kalman Filter (UKF)                 │
│  • DAG Construction (NarrativeStructure)                        │
│  • VAD Affective Trajectory                                     │
│  • RST Analysis (DMRST-Parser, local)                           │
│  • Interpretation Engine (Bayesian Hypothesis Competition)      │
│  • Strategy Selector                                            │
│  • Companion Fade Engine                                        │
│  • Placeholder Restorer                                         │
│  • SQLite (local persistence)                                   │
│                                                                 │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  ZONE B — ENCRYPTED SYNC (Zettelkasten Shadow Memory)           │
│  Abstract behavioral schemas only. No raw text. No names.       │
│  No locations. No specific events.                              │
│                                                                 │
│  • Abstract pattern nodes: {"pattern": "pressure→withdrawal",   │
│    "frequency": "recurring", "thread_id": "uuid"}              │
│  • Encrypted at rest (AES-256)                                  │
│  • Encrypted in transit (TLS 1.3)                               │
│  • Optional user opt-in. Off by default.                        │
│  • Upgrade path: Azure Confidential Computing TEE               │
│    (planned post-launch with institutional backing)             │
│                                                                 │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  ZONE C — EXTERNAL BOUNDED CLOUD                                │
│  Receives ONLY: distilled, anonymized NarrativeStructure JSON   │
│  and behavioral strategy specification.                         │
│  NEVER receives: raw text, PWM, state vector, entity names.     │
│                                                                 │
│  • Groq (LLM inference — language generation only)             │
│  • ElevenLabs (TTS)                                             │
│  • OpenAI Whisper (STT) — receives audio only, not text         │
│  • Chain-of-Agents pattern extraction (Gemini 2.0 Flash)        │
│    — receives abstract Zone B schemas only, on user opt-in      │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**The privacy guarantee:** A user can be fully honest with Sanctuary because
the system that accumulates rich understanding of them (Zone A) never communicates
with the system that has network access (Zone C) except through a stripped,
anonymized intermediary structure. The external model sees a thin slice.
Only the local model sees the whole picture.

